/-
  The no-direction sentences of rdr-config-deep.kompile.kore, all 273 of the class of its tie
  (`test/TieRdrConfigDeep.lean`, `classes`), in one model of the theory, for every interpretation H
  of the parameters: the equations that define a generated symbol (the cell initializers, the
  counter's getter, the sorts' projections), the counter initializer's `functional` axiom, and the
  `functional` axioms of the hooked map functions `_-Map_` (539), `_<=Map_` (540) and `updateMap`
  (834), which no read sentence applies. Run from the package root:
  `lake env lean -j1 test/GenEqsNodirRdrConfigDeep.lean`.

  The text is the construct fixture rdr-config-deep, a configuration of 63 nested cells around
  `<k> $PGM:K </k>`, by K 7.1.337's kompile. Its user module is read as the account reads it
  (`consumedWith`, `Account.lean`): its scan `S = scan m.sentences` block by block (`scan_eq`),
  computed by compiled code (`parse_stages`) and checked by the kernel. The model reads the listed
  equations from the scan's blocks that hold exactly the listed equations (`eqsN`, a sublist of
  `S.eqs`: `eqsN_sub`); the names `E` that `envOf` gives (computed, not checked here) are data for
  the checks (`nodSentEqB` reads them), and the instance holds whatever names they read.

  The sentences are named by index (`AxiomDecl.index`, the text's axiom numbers): `eqIdx` the
  equations (as `Parse.scanEqn` reads each), `funIdx` the constants' `functional` axioms
  (`GenEqs.nodFunctional?`), `funAtIdx` and `funValIdx` the hooked map functions' `functional`
  axioms (`GenEqs.nodFunctionalAt?`). They are the no-direction class of the tie (`listed_class`),
  each applies a symbol Γ lacks (`listed_absent`), and `sents` are the user module's axioms of
  these indices (`sents_eq`).

  Nothing here writes a right side, a value or a `G` by hand but the value of `_<=Map_`. The model
  is the arm's (`GenEqs.model_with_inits_arm`): `G` read from the equations along the cell tree
  (`GenEqs.armG`), the getter and the projections by `GenEqs.armBase`. The names are the tree's
  initializers bottom up (`order`, the presentation's: `order_eq`) and the listed equations' other
  symbols, each borne by no symbol of the semantics (`GenEqs.nodLackedB`), so that no premise of the
  theory names it. The text states nothing of the hooked map functions but that they are
  `functional`, and Γ lacks them: the model gives `_-Map_` and `updateMap` their first argument
  (a map) and `_<=Map_` the value `false` (`GenEqs.nod_instance_funv_lacked`). The sorts of each
  right side are read from the text (`GenEqs.nodTy`, `nodR`) and checked (`nodOrderB`), and each
  listed equation is one of the shapes `GenEqs.nod_eqB` takes (`nodSentEqB`): so each holds at every
  list of values of its variables' sorts (`GenEqs.NodEqn`). The checks read no interpretation, so
  they are decided once on the data and the model is had for every H
  (`GenEqs.nod_instance_funv_lacked_withHooks`), with `FnHyp` under every H as the tie has it
  (`fnHypH`).

  The decisions read names by their codes where they compare them with Γ's symbols (`gSymCodes`,
  `KoreAML.Distinct.strCode`), read the names' sorts from a table checked once (`tbl_ok`,
  `GenEqs.nodR_eq_tbl`) rather than reading the tree below each name again, and are cut into blocks.
-/
